  + Added a copper Operand-Read Bus running from the crossbar east into the DSP multiplier column with a copper direction arrow, completing the read/twiddle/return dataflow triad so the operand-read half of the conflict-free read-modify-write loop is now visible geometry rather than only a connection-graph edge.
  + Rooted the read bus through the crossbar (crossbar -> read_bus -> read_arrow -> bu_mult_3/bu_mult_4) and registered both new ids on pcb_substrate and crossbar_network so the graph stays single-rooted with no dangling ids.
  + Re-materialed all eight lane subtractors (and the exploded subtractor) from dark anodized aluminum to brushed steel so the difference path reads distinct from the adders' sum path at a glance while keeping the symmetric-pair grouping.
  + Shifted the entire exploded butterfly cluster (baseplate, two risers, multiply/add/sub/register) +1.2 m in Z so it no longer sits over the central add/sub lanes 2-4 in the TOP plan view.
